    "fields": {
      "category": "trade_procedure",
      "content": "Standard commercial import procedure via Uganda Revenue Authority customs and URA e-services.\n\nProcedure steps:\n1. Obtain TIN and register importer: Register with URA and obtain a Tax Identification Number before importing.\n2. Prepare shipping documentation: Commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading/airway bill, and certificate of origin.\n3. Customs declaration (ASYCUDA): Submit import declaration through ASYCUDA World via licensed clearing agent.\n4. Pay duties and taxes: Pay import duty, VAT, and any excise at customs before release.\n5. Release and delivery: Goods released after inspection and payment confirmation.\n\nSource: Uganda Trade Portal (https://www.ura.go.ug/en/e-services/efris/)",
      "country_code": "UG",
